  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eritrea Community Based Nutrition Project - DFID</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food insecurity continues to affect households throughout Eritrea whose coping mechanisms have been severely weakened by repeated drought and national political and economic issues. Rising food prices and poor rains are expected to make it even more difficult for households to obtain sufficient food. 

This project will re-establish CAFOD&#x2019;s support to the Catholic Church in Eritrea&#x2019;s nutrition programmes. This 9 month project aims to provide malnourished children under 5 and pregnant and lactating mothers with a supplementary food ration, in order to maintain or improve their nutritional status and prevent deterioration to severe malnutrition and death. The project will work through the Eritrean Catholic Secretariat&#x2019;s (ErCS) network of health clinics alongside the Ministry of Health and Unicef and will be implemented in the worst affected areas across all three Catholic eparchies (dioceses) of Eritrea.</narrative>
  </description>
